From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:45:00 +0000
Subject: pass installation directories at make time

configure computes the installation directories itself and puts them
into config.h (apl_DIR__bin, apl_DIR__pkglib, ...) and, via
AC_CONFIG_FILES, into gnu-apl.d/preferences.  Directories given on the
configure command line are copied verbatim, unexpanded: dh_auto_configure
passes --libdir=${prefix}/lib/<triplet>, so apl --show_lib_dir prints
"${prefix}/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/apl", and NativeFunction.cc looks for
native libraries (lib_file_io.so etc.) there.  Also, preferences.in
sets LIBREF-3/4/5 to @prefix@/lib/apl/wslibN, while wslibN are
installed into $(pkglibdir) = $(libdir)/apl, so with any other
--libdir, e.g. Debian's multiarch libdir, )LIBS shows libraries 3-5 as
missing and )LOAD 5 FILE_IO fails.

Either expand the directories in configure, or substitute them at make
time as the Autoconf manual recommends ("Installation Directory
Variables").  The latter is done here.

The apl_DIR__ macros that the code uses are defined in AM_CPPFLAGS of
src/Makefile.am and src/APs/Makefile.am from $(bindir), $(docdir),
$(sysconfdir), $(pkglibdir) and $(pkgdatadir); configure no longer
computes them.  gnu-apl.d/preferences is generated by sed in
gnu-apl.d/Makefile.am, with @pkglibdir@ and @sysconfdir@ in
preferences.in.  It is installed only from there, and not distributed:
the top-level Makefile.am no longer installs it a second time, and
gnu-apl.d/Makefile.am installs into gnuapldir instead of redefining
distdir, automake's directory for make dist.

Forwarded: no
---
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -476,7 +476,6 @@
                  erlang/Makefile
                  erlang/apl.erl
                  gnu-apl.d/Makefile
-                 gnu-apl.d/preferences
                  HOWTOs/Makefile
                  HOWTOs/Bible/Makefile
                  rpm/Makefile
@@ -819,117 +818,10 @@
